<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>{{ css }}</style></head><body>
<h1>{{ config.report_name }}<br>{{ config.dataset_id }}: objective-aware integration</h1>
<div class="decision"><b>Integration verdict: {{ verdict.integration_verdict }}</b><p>The validation-selected representation is
{{ verdict.selected_representation }} ({{ verdict.selected_strategy }}). Its selected encoders are {{ display_encoders|join(', ') }},
with {{ verdict.fusion_type }} fusion and {{ verdict.training_objective }} objective. Held-out comparisons and uncertainty appear below.</p></div>
<h2>Objective and principal findings</h2>
<p>{{ objective.original_text }}</p>
<p>Allowed supervision: <b>{{ objective.allowed_supervision }}</b>. Primary metrics: {{ objective.primary_metrics|join(', ') }}.
The deterministic planner and templated reporting used no external LLM.</p>
{% if verdict.selected_representation == 'fusion_late' %}<p>Late-fusion training averages the image and clinical branches' class logits.
The exported joint representation concatenates their learned latent vectors; the common logistic probe below is fitted on that concatenation.
The MIL image branch pools frozen tile features, while the clinical branch encodes the allowed table.</p>{% endif %}
<table><thead><tr><th>Representation</th><th>Family</th><th>Dim.</th><th>Macro-F1</th><th>95% CI</th><th>Balanced accuracy</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for row in comparison_rows %}<tr><td>{{ row.model }}</td><td>{{ row.family }}</td><td>{{ row.dimension }}</td><td>{{ row.macro_f1 }}</td><td>{{ row.ci }}</td><td>{{ row.balanced_accuracy }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<p>All rows use the same frozen-embedding logistic probe protocol. End-to-end head predictions are a separate analysis.
The selected model was frozen before test access. Paired bootstrap resampling follows the sample unit recorded in the evidence.</p>
{% if selected_details.end_to_end_head is defined %}<p>The separately evaluated end-to-end head has macro-F1 {{ '%.3f'|format(selected_details.end_to_end_head.macro_f1) }}
and balanced accuracy {{ '%.3f'|format(selected_details.end_to_end_head.balanced_accuracy) }}. The primary comparisons and confidence intervals use the common logistic probe.</p>{% endif %}
<p>Baseline names: view_a uses {{ profile.modalities[0].modality_id }}; view_b uses {{ profile.modalities[1].modality_id }}.
Concatenation uses the scaled feature blocks from both modalities.</p>
<p>Against the best single modality ({{ verdict.comparison_to_best_single_modality.model }}), the selected-minus-reference
macro-F1 difference is {{ '%.3f'|format(verdict.comparison_to_best_single_modality.estimate) }}
(95% CI {{ '%.3f'|format(verdict.comparison_to_best_single_modality.lower) }} to {{ '%.3f'|format(verdict.comparison_to_best_single_modality.upper) }}).
Project decision thresholds are pre-registered in METHOD_NOTES.md and are not external scientific standards.</p>
{% for figure in figures[:1] %}<div class="figure"><img src="{{ figure }}"><p class="caption">Held-out comparison; candidate selection used validation only.</p></div>{% endfor %}
<h2>Data, pairing and cohort</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Modality</th><th>Type</th><th>Samples</th><th>Features</th><th>Missingness/QC</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for m in profile.modalities %}<tr><td>{{ m.modality_id }}</td><td>{{ m.modality_type }}</td><td>{{ m.n_samples }}</td><td>{{ m.n_features }}</td><td>{{ 'sparse counts; missing covariates tracked separately' if m.sparsity else 'see modality-specific QC and clinical missingness artifacts' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<p>Pairing level: {{ profile.pairing.pairing_level }}. All eligible samples were assigned before fitting.
{% for caveat in profile.label_caveats %}{{ caveat }}. {% endfor %}</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Cohort step</th><th>Count</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for key,value in profile.cohort_flow.items() if value is number %}<tr><td>{{ key|replace('_',' ') }}</td><td>{{ value }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<h2>Preprocessing and leakage control</h2>
<p>Fit scope: training only. Preprocessing receipts record fitted identifiers, split hashes, QC thresholds and feature selection.
Neither test data nor target labels fit preprocessing.</p>
{% if preprocessing.modalities is defined %}<table><thead><tr><th>Modality</th><th>Method</th><th>Retained features</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for m in preprocessing.modalities %}<tr><td>{{ m.modality_id }}</td><td>{{ m.method }}</td><td>{{ m.retained_features }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<p>Raw expression counts are retained for count likelihoods. {% for m in preprocessing.modalities if m.first_lsi_depth_correlation is defined %}First-LSI depth correlation: {{ '%.3f'|format(m.first_lsi_depth_correlation) }}; dropped first component: {{ m.drop_first }}.{% endfor %}</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Agent QC cohort step</th><th>Cells</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for key,value in preprocessing.cohort_flow.items() if value is number %}<tr><td>{{ key|replace('_',' ') }}</td><td>{{ value }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}{% for key,value in preprocessing.cohort_flow.by_split.items() %}<tr><td>{{ key }} after QC</td><td>{{ value }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<table><thead><tr><th>QC variable</th><th>Scale</th><th>Lower bound</th><th>Upper bound</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for key,r in preprocessing.thresholds.items() %}<tr><td>{{ key|replace('_',' ') }}</td><td>{{ r.transform if r.transform is defined else 'identity' }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(r.lower) if r.lower is defined else 'Not set' }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(r.upper) if r.upper is defined else 'Not set' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<p>Doublet decision: {{ preprocessing.doublet.reason }} TSS measure: {{ preprocessing.tss_measure }}.</p>
{% if preprocessing.doublet.threshold is defined and preprocessing.doublet.threshold is not none %}<p>Training doublet-score threshold {{ '%.3f'|format(preprocessing.doublet.threshold) }};
predicted training doublet fraction {{ '%.3f'|format(preprocessing.doublet.predicted_training_doublet_fraction) }}. This diagnostic does not exclude cells.</p>{% endif %}
{% else %}<p>Clinical inputs: {{ preprocessing.input_columns|join(', ') }}. {{ preprocessing.imputation }}.
Missingness indicators: {{ preprocessing.missingness_indicators }}. Molecular-derived, outcome, follow-up and treatment variables are excluded from both tabular and templated-text inputs.</p>{% endif %}
{% if wsi is not none %}{% if wsi.example.fixture_only is defined and wsi.example.fixture_only %}<p><b>Synthetic rendering fixture:</b> the following metadata exercise report formatting; they do not claim actual WSI extraction or measured throughput.</p>{% endif %}<p>WSI preprocessing uses per-slide saturation-Otsu segmentation with morphology, followed by physical-coordinate sampling and pixel-level tissue/blur/pen QC.
{{ wsi.tiling.slides_success }} of {{ wsi.tiling.slides_total }} slides produced coordinate stores. Requested fields: {{ wsi.example.tile_size }} pixels at {{ '%.3f'|format(wsi.example.target_mpp) }} µm/px;
the same physical field is resized to each encoder's native input. Stain normalization is disabled.</p>
{% if wsi.coordinate_repairs.count %}<p>After a region-QC failure, {{ wsi.coordinate_repairs.count }} slide received an explicitly logged coordinate repair:
large, nearly uniform, highly saturated edge artifacts were excluded from the segmentation thumbnail before Otsu thresholding.
The raw slide, original coordinates and failure evidence were preserved. Region-QC thresholds and the production tile cap stayed fixed;
no patient was excluded. The evidence bundle records original/repaired coordinate hashes and the postprocessor source.</p>{% endif %}
<p>The measured pilot used {{ wsi.selection.measured_slides }} training slides. The fixed cap is {{ wsi.selection.tile_cap }} tiles/slide, with safety factor {{ wsi.selection.safety_factor }},
projected extraction cost {{ '%.3f'|format(wsi.projected_hours) }} aggregate GPU-hours against the {{ '%.3f'|format(wsi.selection.extraction_hours_envelope) }}-hour envelope.</p>
{% if wsi.selection.operational_constraints is defined %}{% set operation=wsi.selection.operational_constraints %}<p>Before TCGA fitting, the operational queue limit changed the budget-only candidate cap {{ operation.original_budget_only_tile_cap }} to the selected cap above.
Partition {{ operation.partition }} allows {{ '%.3f'|format(operation.wall_hours_per_task) }} hours/task; the feature array runs at most {{ operation.array_parallel }} shard at a time.
The policy retains measured twofold safety plus {{ operation.startup_seconds_per_task }} seconds of initialization allowance per task. All methods use the same production cap.</p>{% endif %}
<table><thead><tr><th>Frozen tile encoder</th><th>Measured encode tiles/second</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for name,rate in wsi.selection.throughput_tiles_per_second.items() %}<tr><td>{{ name }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(rate) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>{% endif %}
<h2>Agent choices and empirical pilot</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Candidate</th><th>Status</th><th>Rule and reason</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for r in applicability %}<tr><td>{{ r.model_id }}</td><td>{{ r.status|replace('_',' ') }}</td><td>{{ r.rule_id }}: {{ r.reason }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<p>Selection rule: {{ decisions.rule_id }}. Validation shortlist: {{ decisions.shortlist|join(', ') }}.
Separate evidence columns preserve utility, alignment, structure, validity, stability and compute rather than an unexplained weighted score.</p>
<p>Pilot caps: {{ config.budget.pilot_seconds }} adapter-fit seconds and {{ config.budget.pilot_epochs }} epochs/iterations;
declared seeds: {{ config.budget.seeds|join(', ') }}. Every eligible candidate is attempted. Import and data-loading time are excluded from adapter fit time.
Shared PCA/LSI fitting occurs in preprocessing; this is not a claim of zero total baseline cost.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Pilot candidate</th><th>Successful / attempted</th><th>Validation macro-F1 (seed SD)</th><th>Recall@10</th><th>Failure evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in pilot_rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.model }}</td><td>{{ r.successful }} / {{ r.attempted }}</td><td>{% if r.validation_macro_f1_mean is not none %}{{ '%.3f'|format(r.validation_macro_f1_mean) }}{% if r.validation_macro_f1_sd is not none %} ({{ '%.3f'|format(r.validation_macro_f1_sd) }}){% endif %}{% else %}Unavailable{% endif %}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(r.validation_recall_at_10) if r.validation_recall_at_10 is not none else 'Not applicable' }}</td><td>{{ r.failure or 'None' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
{% if profile.pairing.pairing_level == 'patient' %}<p>Actual tower fine-tuning is capped at 128 training patients with four cached tiles per patient;
training samples one cached tile per patient step and exported inference uses the first cached tile. This differs from full-cohort frozen-feature MIL and
is recorded as unequal data/capacity access. Clinical templated text adds no information beyond the allowed table.</p>{% endif %}
<h3>Primary-metric differences after freezing</h3>
<table><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Selected minus best single (95% CI)</th><th>Selected minus simple fusion (95% CI)</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for metric,d in verdict.comparison_to_best_single_modality.primary_metric_differences.items() %}{% set f=verdict.comparison_to_simple_fusion_baseline.primary_metric_differences[metric] %}<tr><td>{{ metric }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(d.estimate) }} ({{ '%.3f'|format(d.lower) }}, {{ '%.3f'|format(d.upper) }})</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(f.estimate) }} ({{ '%.3f'|format(f.lower) }}, {{ '%.3f'|format(f.upper) }})</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Seed</th><th>Fit seconds</th><th>Epochs/steps</th><th>Stopping</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for r in final.runs %}<tr><td>{{ r.model_id }}</td><td>{{ r.seed }}</td><td>{{ '%.1f'|format(r.runtime_seconds) }}</td><td>{{ r.epochs_or_steps_completed }}</td><td>{{ r.early_stopping_reason }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
{% if compute_gpu_hours is not none %}<p>Project aggregate GPU time in the saved ledger: {{ '%.3f'|format(compute_gpu_hours) }} GPU-hours{% if ledger_reconciled_utc %} (reconciled {{ ledger_reconciled_utc }}){% endif %}.
This includes both datasets and runtime/throughput acceptance work, rather than only this dataset. The immutable ledger snapshot accompanies this report.</p>{% endif %}
<h2>Representation quality and confounding</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Effective rank</th><th>Leiden ARI</th><th>Leiden NMI</th><th>Alignment</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for name,r in evidence.models.items() %}<tr><td>{{ name }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(r.validity.effective_rank) }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(r.structure.ari) }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(r.structure.nmi) }}</td><td>{% if r.alignment.foscttm is defined %}FOSCTTM {{ '%.3f'|format(r.alignment.foscttm) }}; pool {{ r.alignment.candidate_pool_size }}{% else %}Not applicable{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<p>Graph connectivity, global-distance correlations, each modality's neighborhood preservation, per-class results,
QC/depth or site predictability, seed/subsample stability and modality ablations are saved as distinct evidence categories.</p>
<p>Alignment definitions from the frozen run records:
{% for definition,names in alignment_definitions.items() %}{{ names|join(', ') }}: {{ definition }}. {% endfor %}
A ridge alignment probe uses training pairs to map the first embedding into the second embedding's coordinates; its retrieval scores describe that
inductive cross-view probe. They do not establish that independently learned or single-modality embeddings intrinsically share a coordinate system.</p>
{% if verdict.selected_representation == 'fusion_late' %}<p>The selected late-fusion towers have independent classifiers and no embedding-alignment loss.
Their raw cosine retrieval/FOSCTTM values describe this fitted parameterization and do not identify a semantically aligned cross-modal space.
The integration decision uses the predeclared predictive metrics and modality-contribution evidence.</p>{% endif %}
<table><thead><tr><th>Selected-model class</th><th>Support</th><th>Recall (95% CI)</th><th>OVR AUROC (95% CI where evaluated)</th><th>Graph connectivity</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for label,recall in selected_details.classification.per_class_recall.items() %}{% set rc=evidence.bootstrap.secondary.balanced_accuracy.per_class_intervals[evidence.selected][label] %}<tr><td>{{ label }}</td><td>{{ selected_details.classification.per_class_support[label] }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(recall) }}{% if rc.lower is not none %} ({{ '%.3f'|format(rc.lower) }}, {{ '%.3f'|format(rc.upper) }}){% endif %}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(selected_details.classification.per_class_auroc[label]) if selected_details.classification.per_class_auroc[label] is not none else 'Undefined' }}{% if evidence.bootstrap.secondary.ovr_auroc is defined %}{% set ac=evidence.bootstrap.secondary.ovr_auroc.per_class_intervals[evidence.selected][label] %}{% if ac.lower is not none %} ({{ '%.3f'|format(ac.lower) }}, {{ '%.3f'|format(ac.upper) }}){% endif %}{% endif %}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(selected_details.structure.per_class_graph_connectivity[label]) if label in selected_details.structure.per_class_graph_connectivity else 'Undefined' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<p>These intervals resample the observed test units. A rare class with only correct observed predictions can have a degenerate recall interval;
this does not establish perfect population recall. Interpret class-level estimates together with their support.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Confounding diagnostic</th><th>Held-out score</th><th>Reference</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for key,r in selected_details.confounding.items() %}<tr><td>{{ key }}</td><td>{% if r.applicable is defined and not r.applicable %}Not applicable: {{ r.reason }}{% elif r.test_r_squared is defined %}R² {{ '%.3f'|format(r.test_r_squared) }}{% else %}Site balanced accuracy {{ '%.3f'|format(r.balanced_accuracy) }}{% endif %}</td><td>{% if r.applicable is defined and not r.applicable %}No score defined{% elif r.chance_reference is defined %}Chance {{ '%.3f'|format(r.chance_reference) }}; uniform over training sites{% else %}Train-fitted linear ridge predictor{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
{% if evidence.validity_flags %}<p><b>Validity/confounding cautions:</b> {{ evidence.validity_flags|join('; ') }}</p>{% endif %}
{% for figure in figures[1:] %}<div class="figure"><img src="{{ figure }}"><p class="caption">{{ figure.stem|replace('_',' ') }}.
{% if figure.stem == 'site_umap' %}Sites are grouped using the five largest training-site counts, with other training sites pooled and previously unseen sites separate. UMAP fits training embeddings and transforms test; display only.
{% elif 'umap' in figure.stem %}UMAP is a train-fitted visualization and is not selection evidence.{% else %}Held-out predictions from the frozen model; colors are row-normalized reference-class proportions.{% endif %}</p></div>{% endfor %}
<h2>Downstream analyses and sensitivity</h2>
<p>Executed downstream tasks: {{ objective.downstream_tasks|join(', ') }}. Full machine-readable results accompany this report.</p>
{% if downstream.cross_modal_prediction is defined %}<table><thead><tr><th>RNA→ATAC predictor</th><th>Per-cell AUROC</th><th>Per-cell AUPRC</th><th>Per-peak AUPRC</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for name,m in downstream.cross_modal_prediction.models.items() %}<tr><td>{{ name }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(m.per_cell_auroc) if m.per_cell_auroc is not none else 'undefined' }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(m.per_cell_auprc) if m.per_cell_auprc is not none else 'undefined' }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(m.per_peak_auprc) if m.per_peak_auprc is not none else 'undefined' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<p>Accessibility targets are binarized peaks selected using {{ downstream.cross_modal_prediction.candidate_peak_selection }}.
Held-out ATAC counts and features are masked before prediction. The separately named kNN decoders use each frozen model's RNA-side representation;
the mean AUPRC across cells and the mean AUPRC across peaks summarize different rankings.</p>{% endif %}
{% if downstream.survival is defined %}<p>Exploratory survival status: {{ downstream.survival.status }}.
{% if downstream.survival.c_index is defined %}Held-out C-index {{ '%.3f'|format(downstream.survival.c_index) }};
{% if downstream.survival.lower is not none %}95% CI {{ '%.3f'|format(downstream.survival.lower) }} to {{ '%.3f'|format(downstream.survival.upper) }};{% endif %}
training events {{ downstream.survival.training_events }}, held-out events {{ downstream.survival.test_events }}.
{{ downstream.survival.caveat }}.{% endif %}</p>{% endif %}
<p>Sensitivity analyses: {% for key,r in downstream.sensitivity.items() %}{{ key }}{% if r.status is defined %} ({{ r.status }}){% endif %}; {% endfor %}.
Read their separate metrics and fit scopes in downstream/results.json; unresolved analyses remain explicit.</p>
{% for table in descriptive_tables %}<h3>{{ table.title }}</h3>
<table><thead><tr>{% for label in table.columns %}<th>{{ label }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead><tbody>
{% for row in table.rows %}<tr>{% for value in row %}<td>{{ '%.3f'|format(value) if value is float else value }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>{% endfor %}
<p>Alignment is descriptive where per-modality spaces are defined; baseline projections are reference spaces, not learned contrastive towers.
Masking index 0 denotes the first configured modality and index 1 the second. Seed rows measure training randomness;
neighbor overlap measures adapter refits on 80% training samples while retaining fixed train-only preprocessing.
Nearest-neighbor label agreement uses labeled queries in the declared pool; candidates without a reference label count as nonmatches.
Luminal diagnostics, when present, restrict true labels to LumA/LumB and retain the frozen four-class predictions, including errors into other classes.
They are descriptive subgroup comparisons without separate model selection or subgroup confidence intervals.</p>
{% for figure in extra_figures %}<div class="figure"><img src="{{ figure }}"><p class="caption">{{ figure.stem|replace('_',' ') }}.
{% if figure.stem == 'selected_qc_umap' %}The same joint UMAP coordinates are colored by the recorded QC measurements. Each panel has its own scale; these displays are descriptive and do not separate biological variation from technical effects.
{% elif figure.stem == 'modality_umap' %}Both frozen tower embeddings share one display map, fitted on training RNA and ATAC embeddings and used to transform held-out paired cells. Modality mixing is descriptive; quantitative retrieval and FOSCTTM supply the alignment evidence.
{% elif 'umap' in figure.stem %}UMAP is fitted on training samples and transforms held-out samples; visualization only.
{% elif figure.stem == 'marker_gene_activity' %}Each marker is standardized across the displayed coarse cell groups within each panel: red is higher and blue is lower relative signal. Peak-linked activity is a vendor-annotation proxy, not measured expression or independent label validation.
{% elif figure.stem == 'selected_training_curves' %}Training and validation objectives from the selected frozen run; selection used validation only.
{% elif figure.stem == 'survival_km' %}Exploratory test-set Kaplan–Meier curves with 95% intervals. A penalized Cox model on training-fitted representation PCs defines risk; the training median risk sets the fixed high/low cutoff. This is retrospective stratification, not clinical validation.
{% elif figure.stem.startswith('attention_heatmap_') %}MIL attention on the highest-total-attention slide of the chosen patient; color is scaled to this slide's maximum weight. Cases follow the frozen logistic probe's confidence rule. This is descriptive pooling attention, not validated localization.
{% elif figure.stem.startswith('attention_') %}Top-attended tiles for a highest-confidence correct/incorrect case under the frozen logistic probe. The learned MIL weights describe image pooling, not validated localization.
{% else %}The example-selection rule is recorded in figure_manifest/attention_selection.{% endif %}</p></div>{% endfor %}
<div class="closing"><h2>Permitted interpretation, limitations and reproducibility</h2>
<ul>{% for item in verdict.uncertainty_and_limitations + verdict.discouraged_or_prohibited_uses %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
<p>Representations include sample IDs, split membership, model/checkpoint/preprocessing hashes and embedding definitions.
The GPU ledger, environment locks, run manifests, decision log, split manifest and evidence source map accompany the outputs.</p>
{% if wsi is not none %}<p>Pathology weights are local pinned resources licensed CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0 for academic/noncommercial use; neither those weights
nor fine-tuned derivatives are redistributed. ImageNet features, where used, are labeled separately.</p>{% endif %}
<p class="small">Sources: local data/label/model provenance manifests; pre-registered METHOD_NOTES.md; scvi-tools MultiVI,
muon WNN, MOFA+, paired contrastive objectives and gated MIL implementations documented in the source and environment locks.
Full citations are in the project report and docs/REFERENCES.json.</p></div>
</body></html>
